{"_id":"6a2fef592204ffbc59e5a32e","roadmapSlug":"python-data-analysis","nodeId":"AzsZhpK-wuWtafVFJMhdY","description":"# Lambda Functions\n\nLambda functions are anonymous, single-expression functions defined with the `lambda` keyword. They are used for short, throwaway operations, particularly as arguments to functions like `map()`, `filter()`, and Pandas' `apply()`. For example: `df['col'].apply(lambda x: x * 2)`.","resources":[{"type":"article","title":"Python Lambda","url":"https://www.w3schools.com/python/python_lambda.asp","_id":"6a75d326b0650226a50aeaff"},{"type":"video","title":"Python Lambda Functions Explained","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HQNiSfb795A","_id":"6a75d326b0650226a50aeb00"}],"createdAt":"2026-06-15T12:26:01.034Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-07T12:44:22.099Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[{"_id":"6a5e3360acf8c05faf5e1c2a","title":"DataCamp - Data Analyst with Python","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/QY0dY9"},{"_id":"6a5e3365acf8c05faf5e1ded","title":"DataCamp - Python Data Fundamentals","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/k4V24x"}],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/python-data-analysis/content/AzsZhpK-wuWtafVFJMhdY.md"}